.TH "TreeSitter::Tree" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "treesitter 0.1.0" "treesitter API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
TreeSitter::Tree \- A syntax tree made by \fB\%Parser#parse\fR.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "treesitter"\fR
.sp
\fBclass TreeSitter::Tree\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
A syntax tree made by \fB\%Parser#parse\fR. Edit it with \fB\%edit\fR before passing it back to \fB\%parse\fR as the old tree, so
unchanged parts are reused. Freed when collected; the \fB\%Node\fRs taken from it keep it alive.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef changed_regions(old : Tree) : Array(Region)\fR
Where the syntax differs between \fIold\fR, edited to match this tree\(aqs text, and this tree. Text edited without a
change in structure is not included, so a highlighter also refreshes the edited lines.
.TP 4
\fBdef copy : Tree\fR
An independent copy, cheap to make, for use on another fiber or as a snapshot.
.TP 4
\fBdef edit(edit : Edit) : Nil\fR
Adjusts the tree\(aqs positions for \fIedit\fR, which already happened to the text.
.TP 4
\fBdef root : Node\fR
The root node.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/tree_sitter/tree.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR "TreeSitter" (3cr),
.BR "TreeSitter::Node" (3cr),
.BR "TreeSitter::Parser" (3cr),
.BR "treesitter" (7cr)
